       <narrative xml:lang="EN">07-05-2026: The main result was completion of the Ecosystem Services Shared Value Assessment (ESSVA). This generated a much stronger basis for identifying restoration priorities, understanding livelihood vulnerabilities, and targeting action where pressures on wetlands and communities are most acute. This was reinforced through more than 15 bilateral meetings with government agencies, research institutions, and NGOs, as well as stakeholder dialogue and workshop processes in Khulna and Dhaka, which helped build shared understanding of ecosystem pressures and strengthened willingness for more coordinated landscape action.</narrative>
